It is evening.
Nina says: "See you tomorrow, Maya."
"See you, Nina," I say.
She goes home to her place.
Now I am alone in my new flat.
I look around the living room.
The lamp stands by the window.
The books stand on the shelf.
The plant from Nina also stands in the window.
The photo of my family is on the little table.
My keys now hang by the door.
Everything is in its place.
My new flat is ready.
Quiet and calm.
